From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:43:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: uniform texture handles, f16 pairing, occupancy-target
 knobs

NAK_TEX_UHANDLE (0-2, default 0, SM100+): a bindless texture handle that
is the same in every lane (by NIR's divergence analysis of the texture
and sampler parts) goes in the uniform register field of TLD (1) or of
TEX, TLD and TLD4 (2), opcodes 0xf66, 0xf60, 0xf63, instead of the
second source vector, as in the reference compiler's code: a UGPR pair
(texture index, sampler index) unpacked from NVK's handle, and only with the scalar source form
(.SCR: one or two components per source register, four in all), which
also saves the copies that build contiguous vectors.  An instruction
with more source components keeps the handle in its second vector.  Legalization brings the handle back to
a UGPR with R2UR if NAK moved it to a GPR.

NAK_REMAT_LD_COST (1-63, default 4): what a rematerialized load costs in
the spiller and in the occupancy target's dry run.  NAK_OCC_GPRS (0-255,
default off): a fixed register target for every shader whose natural
count is higher, for sweeps of one shader with dispatch-replay.

NAK_F16_PAIR (default off, SM86+): independent scalar 32-to-16-bit
float conversions in a block are paired into one 2-wide conversion (one
F2FP.PACK_AB from two registers), preferring partners whose first use is
the same operation, so nir_opt_vectorize can pack the 16-bit math that
follows into HFMA2/HADD2/HMUL2.

All of them are in nak_knobs_key2(), so in NVK's pipeline cache keys.
